{"id": "EUVD-2026-95525", "enisaUuid": "a5666612-afff-3711-8463-354a0e5e4e77", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header\n\nhandle_incoming_queue() pulls pull_to bytes into the head before\ncalling eth_type_trans().  pull_to is the length of the first RX slot,\ncapped at RX_COPY_THRESHOLD, and that length comes from the backend.\nNothing checks it against ETH_HLEN.\n\nIf the first slot is shorter than ETH_HLEN and more slots follow, the\nhead ends up shorter than an Ethernet header while skb->len is longer,\nand eth_type_trans() BUG()s in __skb_pull().  If the whole packet is\nshorter than ETH_HLEN, eth_type_trans() reads the header past the end\nof the data instead.\n\nPull at least ETH_HLEN, and drop the packet if that fails, which also\ndrops packets too short to hold an Ethernet header.  This also checks\nthe return value of the pull, which was ignored.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T07:10:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0542d213253eec18785a24b603b28bd385dfe4a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/236a17caebcff31f75bec5ff4136bde2de944e40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72d2f54367895d6e236b9857892e2e6b6036e067", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2b721bc30f40ffa7ccc36a56d4e8990b8c0538e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/089e58805c452e52179482b1025a8e309a57f801"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6q97-4p5q-xv9v", "CVE-2026-98375"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16759317-ee81-3ec4-bbbc-d27eda0e8308", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "23dbeb87-b8e9-3d7d-9300-66d3aa9bba3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d160211965b79de989cf2d170985abeb8da5ec6 <72d2f54367895d6e236b9857892e2e6b6036e067"}, {"id": "32f43ae9-7b03-3520-b30c-d99681eeb528", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.23"}, {"id": "4cba3d1b-00e2-3dcd-ac46-a7bfe91dfb2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d160211965b79de989cf2d170985abeb8da5ec6 <0542d213253eec18785a24b603b28bd385dfe4a5"}, {"id": "ab46be34-4054-30ca-9c41-a22056a9d15c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "b06adab9-0df8-3dc8-87ee-4a22f93171ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ba2ea0dc-bee9-398d-aee3-ab9d3f13b921", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "c0617c48-23d3-311a-a410-54d92db86376", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "d855eaca-1317-382c-803b-65130194caee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "dd6a14a0-f304-3ba2-9ca0-28e2e670547a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d160211965b79de989cf2d170985abeb8da5ec6 <e2b721bc30f40ffa7ccc36a56d4e8990b8c0538e"}, {"id": "e9ca0091-631e-3b94-88b2-21795e6cefa1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d160211965b79de989cf2d170985abeb8da5ec6 <089e58805c452e52179482b1025a8e309a57f801"}, {"id": "ef8ed43a-3310-3f94-9313-aaeec724bb4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0d160211965b79de989cf2d170985abeb8da5ec6 <236a17caebcff31f75bec5ff4136bde2de944e40"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "07e1d4b7-3106-3232-90f8-5d21d8c51f3f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}